welcome to Walt Disney World the most  magical place on Earth and every kid's  Paradise  okay maybe not let's discuss why Disney  World and all the Disney theme parks  were not made for children now you might  be thinking wait isn't Disney the  happiest place on Earth isn't it  specifically designed for kids to have  fun and make magical memories well not  really while it's true that Disney World  and the other Disney theme parks are  certainly family friendly and geared  towards providing entertainment and  enjoyment for all ages the truth is that  they weren't initially designed with  kids in mind the idea for Disneyland  came from Walt Disney himself who wanted  to create a place where adults could  experience the same sense of wonder and  joy that children do he thought of the  park as his own personal playground from  the beginning he made it as a place  where adults would want to go and  perhaps bring their kids along now  though it's important to understand that  Disney is a massive multi-billion dollar  Corporation and like any Corporation its  primary goal is to make money obviously  there are many different ways that  Disney World can generate Revenue but  one of the biggest is through ticket  sales and who buys tickets to Disney  World adults in fact many adults even  visit the park with without children or  with children who are too young to  remember the trip myself included these  adult guests can bring in just as much  revenue as kids can and Disney knows it  also let's consider the price Disney  World tickets are not cheap and they  only seem to be getting more and more  expensive if you're a parent trying to  bring your family to Disney World you're  probably gonna have to save up for a  while before you can afford it this  means that Disney World is more geared  towards those with the financial means  to afford it rather than larger families  with children who might not have the  disposable income to pay for such an  expensive vacation now before you start  thinking I'm crazy hear me out Disney is  known for its magical child-friendly  atmosphere but if you take a closer look  you'll see that there are actually quite  a few things about Disney World that are  not necessarily geared towards kids  there are a lot of adult oriented  attractions and experiences at Disney  world that kids might not be interested  in for example there are numerous fine  dining restaurants wine tastings and  nightlife options at the resort that are  more geared towards adults there are  also adult themed areas like the Disney  Springs shopping district that kids  might not find very exciting one of the  biggest draws to Disney World though is  Epcot and especially how you can drink  around the world at Epcot  and park has a series of pavilions made  to look like and sponsored by other  countries such as Germany Italy Mexico  and Canada and each of these Pavilions  you can drink the country's alcoholic  beverage of choice and move on to the  next one thus allowing you to drink  around the world another reason that  Disney World might not be entirely for  kids is that it's simply too big and too  complex for them to fully appreciate the  Disney World Resort spans over 40 square  miles or twice the size of Manhattan and  it includes four separate theme parks  two water parks and dozens of hotels  restaurants and other attractions that's  a lot of ground to cover and it can be  overwhelming for kids and even adults to  try to see and do everything also if you  like what you're seeing hit that  subscribe button for more videos like  this at Disney World the theme park  experience itself can be overwhelming  for young children too with long lines  crowds and the need to stay with a  parent or Guardian at all times this can  make it difficult for kids to fully  enjoy the experience making it more  suitable for adults one thing that  always stands out to me at Disney World  though is the immersion in every Park  every land every ride the one thing that  never fails to amaze me is how well they  immerse you into the environment take  Star Wars Galaxy's Edge for example you  feel like you're really in the Star Wars  Galaxy building lightsabers and piloting  the Millennium Falcon or take Pandora  the world of Avatar it really feels like  you're in James Cameron's World riding a  Banshee or gazing at the Pandora and  floating mountains this type of  immersion is something kids definitely  wouldn't be able to pick up on no this  was brought to the Disney parks  specifically for adults to appreciate  additionally some other rides and  attractions at Disney World are simply  not suitable for young children for  example the Tower of Terror and Space  Mountain are both thrilling rides that  may be too intense for younger kids  speaking of younger kids it really kind  of sucks in some ways to go to Disney  World with them don't get me wrong I  loved seeing my son waddle up to Mickey  Mouse and hold his hand and in seeing  the smile on his face while he watched  the nighttime fireworks but the days are  long and hard whenever you bring a child  you have to account for potty breaks in  nap time going home early not being able  to ride the big rides pushing a stroller  and so much more as an adult you don't  have to worry about any of those things  without kids along for the ride you can  go at your own pace see what you want to  see ride what you want to ride drink  what you want to drink I've been on  trips both with and without kids and let  me tell you the trips without kids are  much more relaxing so while Disney World  may seem like it's all about the kids on  the outside there are actually a lot of  things at the park that are more geared  towards adults that being said there is  still plenty of child-friendly  attractions and experiences at Disney  World and kids can certainly have a  great time at the park but it's  important to remember that Disney World  was not solely made for children and  there are many aspects of the park that  are geared towards a more adult audience  ultimately it's up to each individual  guest to decide what they want to  experience while they're there and  whether they think Disney World is for  kids or for adults  foreign  [Music]
 

